{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791987630361,"sessionID":"ses_ec53aa391ffe0Yfcjlez04t8W4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5da2eb7a75f54c66a093531d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-arc-kill2\\initiatives\\distribute\\phases\\phase-10-spec.md"},"output":"<path>E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-arc-kill2\\initiatives\\distribute\\phases\\phase-10-spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Phase 10 — `uninstall`, `init` for every harness, the consumer registry, the launch slot, the radar; retro and seal\n2: \n3: **Goal (one line):** `arc uninstall` removes exactly what the manifest lists, `arc init` with no `--target` renders every harness and registers the project locally, a new venture is born through the launch `core` slot with every harness, and a weekly ₹0 radar reports consumer drift without writing to any consumer.\n4: **Appetite:** 1 day — blown appetite = cut scope or kill, never extend silently\n5: **Depends on:** phase-09\n6: **REQs closed here:** REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19\n7: \n8: ## Scope\n9: \n10: 1. `arc uninstall [--dir D] [--force]` (ADR-2024) with the mutant-manifest refusals and the `hooks_path_set` arms.\n11: 2. `arc init` with no `--target` = the union of the four targets under ADR-2023's owner rule, one v2 manifest; registry append/remove in `$ARC_PRIVATE_DIR/consumers.json` (ADR-2026); `outdated --all`.\n12: 3. Launch `core` slot calling `bin/arc.mjs init --dir <venture>`, after the launch lane confirms name and tier (paste-ready prompt to that session; A-17).\n13: 4. `distribute-radar` job (`hq.jobs.yaml` row `cadence: daily@07:45` self-throttled to 7 days like `launch-watch`, `processes/distribute-radar.process.yaml` `job_stub: true`, `hq.policy.yaml` row, `.claude/scripts/hq/jobs/distribute-radar.mjs`) emitting one path-free `metric.observed`.\n14: 5. The single cycle PR merged after CI green; from the main clone: tag `v0.2.0` on the merge commit (owner's explicit OK for that push), the kill check re-run on a clone of merged `main` ($0.05), the radar run once for real with its receipt found in `events/`; then retro, evidence bundle, HISTORY entry, lane IDLE.\n15: \n16: ## Exit criteria (Definition of Done)\n17: \n18: - [ ] REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19 bats green on all 3 CI legs per job\n19: - [ ] attack pass (`/arc-attack`, max 2 rounds), findings fixed or ledgered\n20: - [ ] retro + seal; tracker updated\n21: \n22: ## Verification plan\n23: \n24: - Coarse (refined at phase start via `/arc-change`): `tests/distribute-lifecycle.bats` gains uninstall / init-all / registry arms, `tests/distribute-radar.bats` hashes consumer dirs before and after; live demo = a launch scaffold fixture born with every harness, then `arc uninstall` leaving its unmanaged files byte-identical.\n25: \n26: ## Rabbit holes in this phase\n27: \n28: - Registry paths leaking into the spine or any tracked file: the radar payload carries counts only.\n29: \n30: ## Out of scope for this phase\n31: \n32: `upgrade --all` (no-go) · `npm publish` (no-go).\n33: \n34: ## Your-setup / pending\n35: \n36: Launch-lane answer on slot name, tier and `launch-coverage` row, requested at P08 close; no answer by P10 start = clause owed, not blocked. The owner's explicit OK for the `v0.2.0` tag push.\n37: \n38: ## Non-negotiables (verbatim from PLAN)\n39: \n40: - The Claude source (`.claude/commands/*.md`, `.claude/agents/*.md`, `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/hooks/`, `.mcp.json`) is not moved, renamed or reformatted; the only source edits this cycle are `arc-ship.md`'s fence and step 4 (ADR-2027), goldened in the same PR (ADR-2001).\n41: - No prose fallback: a construct a target cannot express is dropped only where the matrix cell says so, otherwise `[unsupported]` by name (ADR-2001, ADR-2003).\n42: - Merge-time is the truth: nothing is enforced only in a Claude Code hook, and a git hook is never called the gate (ADR-2002, ADR-2013, ADR-2015).\n43: - `AGENTS.md` is the brain and is never a render output; `CLAUDE.md` only imports it plus marked Claude-only blocks (ADR-2007, ADR-2023).\n44: - Every lifecycle verb reads the manifest first and writes or removes only paths it names; a path that escapes the project is refused by name (ADR-2024).\n45: - No consumer path in any tracked file, spine payload included (ADR-2026).\n46: - A pushed tag is never moved or deleted (ADR-2025).\n47: - Code lives in `engine` beside `arc-compile` and gates in `core`; no second compiler, no second walker (ADR-2012); new gates run as bats inside existing CI jobs (ADR-2016).\n48: - Two-surface adversarial pass via `/arc-attack` (ADR-0226) per phase, logic and boundary, carrying `initiatives/distribute/fixed-defects.md`; the author is never the attacker; max 2 rounds (ADR-2011).\n49: - Zero npm deps; no `npm publish`; no public README rewrite; no bash port (ADR-2008); no model, driver, router, profile or tier change (ADR-2006).\n50: - Tests run on CI only, and every fixture asserts it RAN before asserting what it printed.\n\n(End of file - total 50 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Phase 10 — `uninstall`, `init` for every harness, the consumer registry, the launch slot, the radar; retro and seal\n\n**Goal (one line):** `arc uninstall` removes exactly what the manifest lists, `arc init` with no `--target` renders every harness and registers the project locally, a new venture is born through the launch `core` slot with every harness, and a weekly ₹0 radar reports consumer drift without writing to any consumer.\n**Appetite:** 1 day — blown appetite = cut scope or kill, never extend silently\n**Depends on:** phase-09\n**REQs closed here:** REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19\n\n## Scope\n\n1. `arc uninstall [--dir D] [--force]` (ADR-2024) with the mutant-manifest refusals and the `hooks_path_set` arms.\n2. `arc init` with no `--target` = the union of the four targets under ADR-2023's owner rule, one v2 manifest; registry append/remove in `$ARC_PRIVATE_DIR/consumers.json` (ADR-2026); `outdated --all`.\n3. Launch `core` slot calling `bin/arc.mjs init --dir <venture>`, after the launch lane confirms name and tier (paste-ready prompt to that session; A-17).\n4. `distribute-radar` job (`hq.jobs.yaml` row `cadence: daily@07:45` self-throttled to 7 days like `launch-watch`, `processes/distribute-radar.process.yaml` `job_stub: true`, `hq.policy.yaml` row, `.claude/scripts/hq/jobs/distribute-radar.mjs`) emitting one path-free `metric.observed`.\n5. The single cycle PR merged after CI green; from the main clone: tag `v0.2.0` on the merge commit (owner's explicit OK for that push), the kill check re-run on a clone of merged `main` ($0.05), the radar run once for real with its receipt found in `events/`; then retro, evidence bundle, HISTORY entry, lane IDLE.\n\n## Exit criteria (Definition of Done)\n\n- [ ] REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19 bats green on all 3 CI legs per job\n- [ ] attack pass (`/arc-attack`, max 2 rounds), findings fixed or ledgered\n- [ ] retro + seal; tracker updated","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-arc-kill2\\initiatives\\distribute\\phases\\phase-10-spec.md","text":"# Phase 10 — `uninstall`, `init` for every harness, the consumer registry, the launch slot, the radar; retro and seal\n\n**Goal (one line):** `arc uninstall` removes exactly what the manifest lists, `arc init` with no `--target` renders every harness and registers the project locally, a new venture is born through the launch `core` slot with every harness, and a weekly ₹0 radar reports consumer drift without writing to any consumer.\n**Appetite:** 1 day — blown appetite = cut scope or kill, never extend silently\n**Depends on:** phase-09\n**REQs closed here:** REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19\n\n## Scope\n\n1. `arc uninstall [--dir D] [--force]` (ADR-2024) with the mutant-manifest refusals and the `hooks_path_set` arms.\n2. `arc init` with no `--target` = the union of the four targets under ADR-2023's owner rule, one v2 manifest; registry append/remove in `$ARC_PRIVATE_DIR/consumers.json` (ADR-2026); `outdated --all`.\n3. Launch `core` slot calling `bin/arc.mjs init --dir <venture>`, after the launch lane confirms name and tier (paste-ready prompt to that session; A-17).\n4. `distribute-radar` job (`hq.jobs.yaml` row `cadence: daily@07:45` self-throttled to 7 days like `launch-watch`, `processes/distribute-radar.process.yaml` `job_stub: true`, `hq.policy.yaml` row, `.claude/scripts/hq/jobs/distribute-radar.mjs`) emitting one path-free `metric.observed`.\n5. The single cycle PR merged after CI green; from the main clone: tag `v0.2.0` on the merge commit (owner's explicit OK for that push), the kill check re-run on a clone of merged `main` ($0.05), the radar run once for real with its receipt found in `events/`; then retro, evidence bundle, HISTORY entry, lane IDLE.\n\n## Exit criteria (Definition of Done)\n\n- [ ] REQ-15, REQ-18, REQ-19 bats green on all 3 CI legs per job\n- [ ] attack pass (`/arc-attack`, max 2 rounds), findings fixed or ledgered\n- [ ] retro + seal; tracker updated\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- Coarse (refined at phase start via `/arc-change`): `tests/distribute-lifecycle.bats` gains uninstall / init-all / registry arms, `tests/distribute-radar.bats` hashes consumer dirs before and after; live demo = a launch scaffold fixture born with every harness, then `arc uninstall` leaving its unmanaged files byte-identical.\n\n## Rabbit holes in this phase\n\n- Registry paths leaking into the spine or any tracked file: the radar payload carries counts only.\n\n## Out of scope for this phase\n\n`upgrade --all` (no-go) · `npm publish` (no-go).\n\n## Your-setup / pending\n\nLaunch-lane answer on slot name, tier and `launch-coverage` row, requested at P08 close; no answer by P10 start = clause owed, not blocked. The owner's explicit OK for the `v0.2.0` tag push.\n\n## Non-negotiables (verbatim from PLAN)\n\n- The Claude source (`.claude/commands/*.md`, `.claude/agents/*.md`, `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/hooks/`, `.mcp.json`) is not moved, renamed or reformatted; the only source edits this cycle are `arc-ship.md`'s fence and step 4 (ADR-2027), goldened in the same PR (ADR-2001).\n- No prose fallback: a construct a target cannot express is dropped only where the matrix cell says so, otherwise `[unsupported]` by name (ADR-2001, ADR-2003).\n- Merge-time is the truth: nothing is enforced only in a Claude Code hook, and a git hook is never called the gate (ADR-2002, ADR-2013, ADR-2015).\n- `AGENTS.md` is the brain and is never a render output; `CLAUDE.md` only imports it plus marked Claude-only blocks (ADR-2007, ADR-2023).\n- Every lifecycle verb reads the manifest first and writes or removes only paths it names; a path that escapes the project is refused by name (ADR-2024).\n- No consumer path in any tracked file, spine payload included (ADR-2026).\n- A pushed tag is never moved or deleted (ADR-2025).\n- Code lives in `engine` beside `arc-compile` and gates in `core`; no second compiler, no second walker (ADR-2012); new gates run as bats inside existing CI jobs (ADR-2016).\n- Two-surface adversarial pass via `/arc-attack` (ADR-0226) per phase, logic and boundary, carrying `initiatives/distribute/fixed-defects.md`; the author is never the attacker; max 2 rounds (ADR-2011).\n- Zero npm deps; no `npm publish`; no public README rewrite; no bash port (ADR-2008); no model, driver, router, profile or tier change (ADR-2006).\n- Tests run on CI only, and every fixture asserts it RAN before asserting what it printed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":50,"totalLines":50,"truncated":false}},"title":"initiatives\\distribute\\phases\\phase-10-spec.md","time":{"start":1791987630331,"end":1791987630356}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me read the active phase spec (phase-10) for its DoD + Verification plan, and check the latest git log for distribute-specific work. The PROGRESS.md \"Now\" is a bit stale — it says \"Next step: push P08 + P09 once\" but the done-log already covers P09/P10 built, attack done, CI runs, real-system checks. The phase 10 evidence shows demo.md exists and transcripts for kill-main-arc-resume (from phase-10 evidence). Actually the phase-10 evidence has `kill-main-arc-resume.jsonl` — that's the seal re-run perhaps? Let me check.\n\nAlso the burn is 2.25d of 4d cap (~56%). 50% tripwire: REQ-16 arms green on CI read on `e08d759f`. The burn says \"~56%... 50% tripwire: REQ-16 arms green on CI is read on e08d759f. Kill checkpoint answered YES; 50% tripwire at day 2.\"\n\nWait, appetite: 4d cap, 3d planned. Burn 2.25d = 56%. The 50% tripwire was at day 2 — REQ-16 (outdated fixtures) must be green on CI. The done-log says CI found 2 issues on first push 9443de57, both fixed in e08d759f. So is the tripwire met? Need to check CI status for the current head.\n\nNote the last commit is b478b743 which is the merged PR #419 \"feat(distribute): Cycle 3 -- self-render, outdated/upgrade/tags, init for every harness, uninstall, radar (REQ-14..19) (#419)\". So everything was merged! Wait but PROGRESS says phases 08-10 are \"🔨 built\" not closed, and the plan said \"merged once at cycle end\". Hmm — the commit b478b743 is on main and merged PR #419. But the PROGRESS.md phases table shows them as 🔨 built, not ✅. And there's no phase done log for P09/P10 closes.\n\nWait, actually let me re-read. The most recent commit b478b743 \"feat(distribute): Cycle 3 -- ... (REQ-14..19) (#419)\" — that merged all of Cycle 3's work to main. But PROGRESS.md \"Now\" says \"Next step: push P08 + P09 once, read CI per job (50% tripwire = REQ-16 arms green), fix what CI finds, then Phase 10.\" That's stale relative to the done-log which covers P10 built and attack. Actually the done-log is quite complete: P08, P08 attack, P09 built, P10 built, P09/P10 attack + real checks. So the \"Now\" section wasn't updated to \"merge and close phases\" — it says next step is push P08+P09 which already happened.\n\nHmm, but there's the phase-10 evidence \"kill-main-arc-resume.jsonl\" transcripts — those look like the seal re-run on merged main. Let me look at phase-10 demo.md and the transcripts.\n\nActually, hold on. The evidence at phase-10 includes `kill-main-arc-resume.jsonl` — this might be the \"re-run once at seal on a clone of the merged main\" from REQ-14. And PROGRESS done-log says nothing about it. So the PROGRESS.md is stale relative to latest work — the working tree has untracked evidence/phase-10/transcripts/ files not committed.\n\nLet me check:\n1. phase-10-spec.md (DoD + Verification plan) — active phase.\n2. The untracked transcripts dir contents.\n3. git log for the branch — everything already merged to main, so the cycle is arguably at seal stage.\n\nWait — actually let me reconsider. The phases 08-10 status in PROGRESS table are 🔨 \"built\" — the seal (retro, closing phases, merging) happens at cycle end. Commit b478b743 already appears to be that merge (#419) of all the REQ-14..19 work. But PROGRESS phases not flipped ✅. So the remaining work: close phases 08-10 via /arc-phase-done, run retro, seal cycle. But phase-10 done-log mentions radar + retro + seal as part of phase 10 scope.\n\nHmm, wait — look at phase-10 table row: \"`uninstall` + `init` default-all + registry + launch slot + radar; retro + seal (REQ-15, 18, 19)\". So phase 10 includes retro + seal. The PROGRESS burn line mentions the seal re-run.\n\nLet me check the phase-10 evidence directory more, and read phase-10-spec.md. Also check whether the transcripts are the kill re-run. Let me also look at what state/.claude/state dir houses snapshots — none found. The resume command says \"the latest `.claude/state/` snapshot (PreCompact hook)\" — maybe it doesn't exist for this repo. Fine — PROGRESS.md is the source of truth.\n\nLet me read phase-10-spec.md and the demo.md / kill-main-arc-resume transcript.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_13ac93fff001fpzvRlereIsPJR","sessionID":"ses